{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
  "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Kent L. Richland",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under the less restrictive constitutional standards applied when government acts as employer, as opposed to sovereign, there was no Fourth Amendment violation here. First, Ontario Police Sergeant Jeff Quon had no reasonable expectation of privacy vis-\u00e0-vis the Ontario Police Department in text messages on his department-issued pager in light of the operational realities of his workplace, which included the explicit no privacy in text messages policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The written policy? (Laughter.)"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And one of the chiefs, out of salacious interest, decides: I'm going to just go in and get those texts, those messages, because I just have a prurient interest. Does that officer have any expectation of privacy that his boss won't just listen in out of prurient interest?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Millions of employees today use technologies of their -- of their employers under policies established by those employers. When a government employer has a no-privacy policy in place that governs the use of those technologies, ad hoc statements by a non-policy member cannot create a reasonable expectation of privacy. Put most simply, the computer help desk cannot supplant the chief's desk. That simple, clear rule should have decided this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, California v. Greenwood was a question of -- of a Fourth Amendment standard that had to be nationwide. So you say it's the same -- same thing here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Mr. Katyal)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Absolutely, Justice Kennedy. I don't disagree with that. I think the only question is, if the -- if I understand your question it\u2019s, does a Federal statute about privacy somehow matter to the Fourth Amendment analysis about reasonable expectations of privacy? And there our contention is, no; it\u2019s precisely because Congress enacted the Stored Communications Act to fill gaps in Fourth Amendment law. That -- that's why it's enacted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents (Dieter Dammeier)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF DIETER DAMMEIER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: You may have an argument that the nature of the policy here and all of the activities related to it don't prove an operational reality of privacy, but I don't know why -- you want a flat rule that says once you have a written policy, there\u2019 no expectation of privacy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Can I ask you this question"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DAMMEIER: There were -- there were a large number on-duty. I think it was broken down to where the average was 27 in a work shift and the most on one day was 80."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF KENT L. RICHARDS ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Mr. Richland, do you take any position on whether Jerilyn Quon, April Florio, and Steve Trujillo stand in the same position as Sergeant Quon insofar as this lawsuit is concerned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Richland",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. RICHLAND: We do, with respect -- in at least one respect, and that is: If Sergeant Quon loses, then we think the other plaintiffs must also lose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So you have to get into who owned --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You sure you want to live with that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1332",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "92e1705c4c0b3a353c8b006756ecb6aa840295536a31f13499e621e68ccf2305",
      "evidence_id": "ev-92e1705c4c0b-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
